---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Agentic Ecosystems
permalink: /
---
{#- The home page. Every term, product and specification comes from `_data/ecosystemMap.json5`, generated from the
    backpack's knowledge map; the only words written here say what each page is for. #}
{%- import "macros/map.njk" as m %}
{%- set map = ecosystemMap %}

<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  <div class="container">
    <h1 id="page-title">{{ site.title }}</h1>
    <p class="lede">A reference map of agentic ecosystems: the terms the field uses, the specifications that connect its parts, and the products that play each part.</p>
    <p>{{ map.products.length }} products are read against {{ map.capabilities.length }} capabilities, {{ map.glossary.length }} terms are defined, and {{ map.specifications.length }} specifications are set out, every fact citing its source and the date it was read.</p>
    {{ m.siteDraftNotice(map.source, "This reference is generated from the Knowledge Islands backpack's knowledge map.") }}
    {#- Image slot 2, the ecosystem map at a glance (docs/design/image-brief.md). #}
    {% imageSlot "ecosystem-map", "The agentic ecosystem at a glance: models, agent harnesses, agent hosts and clients, the specifications between them, and where the mapped products sit." %}
  </div>
</section>

<section id="start" class="band" aria-labelledby="start-title">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 id="start-title">Start here</h2>
    <ul class="product-grid">
      <li class="card"><p class="product-name"><a href="/overview/">Overview</a></p><p class="product-note">What an agentic ecosystem is, its layers from the model to the client, and the parts products play.</p></li>
      <li class="card"><p class="product-name"><a href="/glossary/">Glossary</a></p><p class="product-note">A page for each term, with what each vendor calls it and the products that are an instance of it.</p></li>
      <li class="card"><p class="product-name"><a href="/specifications/">Specifications</a></p><p class="product-note">The open specifications the terms rest on, each with its parts and the products that conform to it.</p></li>
      <li class="card"><p class="product-name"><a href="/matrix/">Capability matrix</a></p><p class="product-note">Every product against every capability, each cell linked to its evidence.</p></li>
      <li class="card"><p class="product-name"><a href="/crosswalk/">Crosswalk</a></p><p class="product-note">Each term beside the words each vendor uses for it.</p></li>
      <li class="card"><p class="product-name"><a href="/how-to-read/">How to read this</a></p><p class="product-note">What the values mean, where the facts come from, and how drafts are marked.</p></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="terms" class="band band-inset" aria-labelledby="terms-title">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 id="terms-title">Terms</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">The industry's terms, in reading order, each building on the ones before it. Each links its glossary page.</p>
    <dl class="term-grid">
      {%- for term in map.glossary | whereEq("kind", "industry") %}
      <div class="card" id="home-term-{{ term.slug }}">
        <dt><a href="{{ term.url }}">{{ term.label }}</a>{% if term.status != "agreed" %} {{ m.statusBadge(term.status) }}{% endif %}</dt>
        <dd><p>{{ term.summaryHtml | safe }}</p></dd>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="products" class="band" aria-labelledby="products-title">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 id="products-title">Products</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Every product mapped so far, with the terms its card says it is an instance of. One product may be several. The <a href="/overview/#roles">overview</a> groups them by part.</p>
    <ul class="product-grid">
      {%- for product in map.products %}
      <li class="card" id="product-{{ product.slug }}">
        <p class="product-name"><a href="/products/{{ product.slug }}/">{{ product.name }}</a> {{ m.statusBadge(product.status) }}</p>
        <p class="product-maker">{{ product.vendor }} · reviewed {{ product.reviewed | longDate }}</p>
        {%- if product.instanceOf.length %}
        <ul class="roles" aria-label="An instance of">
          {%- for card in product.instanceOf %}
          <li class="badge">{{ card.label }}</li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
        {%- endif %}
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="specifications" class="band band-inset" aria-labelledby="specs-title">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 id="specs-title">Specifications</h2>
    <dl class="term-grid">
      {%- for spec in map.specifications %}
      <div class="card">
        <dt><a href="{{ spec.url }}">{{ spec.label }}</a>{% if spec.status != "agreed" %} {{ m.statusBadge(spec.status) }}{% endif %}</dt>
        <dd><p>{{ spec.summaryHtml | safe }}</p></dd>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>
